From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:19:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: enable JPEG decoding on suniv, 4:2:0 only,
 without requests

Enable the JPEG decoder of the previous patch on the suniv F1C100s
variant (VE 0x1663, F1C100s/F1C200s): its manual lists "JPEG decode up to
16384x16384" for the VE, though it documents no VE register.

Take only 4:2:0 JPEGs on the VEs with tiled output only (the A10
generation and suniv). They do not downsample to 4:2:0: a 4:4:4 JPEG
comes out as 4:2:2, as the upstream series' cover letter says of the A10,
and its chroma is twice what the NV12 CAPTURE buffer holds. On the
F1C200s the engine wrote 32 KiB past the end of a 256x256 picture's
buffer. 4:2:2 has no downsampling at all there.

A whole JPEG needs no controls, so let it be queued without a request:
the OUTPUT queue no longer requires requests, and cedrus_qbuf() still
returns -EBADR for an OUTPUT buffer without one when the format is not
JPEG, as Jernej Skrabec asked in review of the upstream series' patch 4/4
(which dropped the requirement for every codec): the stateless codecs do
not decode correctly without their per-frame controls.

The picture comes out as NV12_32L32 (32x32 tiles) like the other codecs,
since this variant has no CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_UNTILED.

Tested on the F1C200s with tools/cedrus_jpeg_test.c: 256x256 baseline
4:2:0 tiles decode in 1.26 ms on average (submit to dequeue) and match a
libjpeg decode (PSNR Y 69 dB, Cb/Cr 48-55 dB); a 4:4:4 one is refused
with the ERROR flag; an H.264 buffer without a request still gets EBADR.
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c   |  1 +
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c  | 15 +++++++++++
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
index 3e7e364..a893be7 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -653,6 +653,7 @@ static const struct cedrus_variant sun50i_h6_cedrus_variant = {
 
 static const struct cedrus_variant suniv_f1c100s_cedrus_variant = {
 	.capabilities	= CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_MPEG2_DEC |
+			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_JPEG_DEC |
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_H264_DEC,
 	.quirks		= CEDRUS_QUIRK_EXTERNAL_PRED_BUFFERS |
 			  CEDRUS_QUIRK_NO_DRAM_MODE_CONFIG,
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c
index 1e8978e..9e1d0b4 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_jpeg.c
@@ -239,6 +239,21 @@ static int cedrus_jpeg_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The VEs with tiled output only (the A10 generation, suniv) do not
+	 * downsample to 4:2:0: they turn 4:4:4 into 4:2:2 and leave 4:2:2 as
+	 * it is, whose chroma is twice what the NV12 CAPTURE buffer holds, and
+	 * the engine writes on past its end (seen on the F1C200s: 32 KiB past
+	 * a 256x256 picture). Take only 4:2:0 there.
+	 */
+	if (subsampling != VE_DEC_MPEG_TRIGGER_CHROMA_FMT_420 &&
+	    !cedrus_is_capable(ctx, CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_UNTILED)) {
+		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev,
+			 "only 4:2:0 JPEGs on this VE (subsampling %06x)\n",
+			 index);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	ctx->codec.jpeg.subsampling = subsampling;
 
 	/* Activate MPEG engine and select JPEG subengine. */
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 7dc7ca5..a887e37 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -419,6 +419,23 @@ static int cedrus_s_fmt_vid_out(struct file *file, void *priv,
 	return cedrus_s_fmt_vid_out_p(cedrus_file2ctx(file), &f->fmt.pix);
 }
 
+static int cedrus_qbuf(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_buffer *buf)
+{
+	struct cedrus_ctx *ctx = cedrus_file2ctx(file);
+
+	/*
+	 * The OUTPUT queue no longer requires requests because of JPEG:
+	 * keep requiring them for the stateless codecs, which do not
+	 * decode correctly without their per-frame controls.
+	 */
+	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(buf->type) &&
+	    ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG &&
+	    !(buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_REQUEST_FD))
+		return -EBADR;
+
+	return v4l2_m2m_ioctl_qbuf(file, priv, buf);
+}
+
 const struct v4l2_ioctl_ops cedrus_ioctl_ops = {
 	.vidioc_querycap		= cedrus_querycap,
 
@@ -434,7 +451,7 @@ const struct v4l2_ioctl_ops cedrus_ioctl_ops = {
 
 	.vidioc_reqbufs			= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_reqbufs,
 	.vidioc_querybuf		= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_querybuf,
-	.vidioc_qbuf			= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_qbuf,
+	.vidioc_qbuf			= cedrus_qbuf,
 	.vidioc_dqbuf			= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_dqbuf,
 	.vidioc_prepare_buf		= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_prepare_buf,
 	.vidioc_create_bufs		= v4l2_m2m_ioctl_create_bufs,
@@ -626,7 +643,11 @@ int cedrus_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,
 	src_vq->lock = &ctx->dev->dev_mutex;
 	src_vq->dev = ctx->dev->dev;
 	src_vq->supports_requests = true;
-	src_vq->requires_requests = true;
+	/*
+	 * A whole JPEG needs no controls, so it may be queued without a
+	 * request; the stateless codecs still need one (cedrus_qbuf).
+	 */
+	src_vq->requires_requests = false;
 
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(src_vq);
 	if (ret)
